# ---- Data -------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw downloads are normally NEVER committed: some sources (DrugBank full
# release) are licence-restricted, and all of them are large + reproducible
# from code.
#
# EXCEPTION: data/raw/drugbank.tab.gz (TDC DDI benchmark, PyTDC 1.1.15,
# downloaded 2026-08-24, 42 MB uncompressed, CC BY-NC 4.0). The agent
# container has no egress to dataverse.harvard.edu, so the file cannot be
# re-downloaded there. Committed gzipped because GitHub's web uploader
# caps single files at 25 MB. See DATA_PROVENANCE.md.
# Note: the pattern must be data/raw/* — an ignored *directory* is never
# descended into, so a negation on a file inside it would not apply.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/raw/drugbank.tab.gz

data/processed/
data/external/
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/external/.gitkeep

# ---- Artefacts --------------------------------------------------------
runs/
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.ckpt
# reports/figures/ is a committed artefact of Phase A
reports/*.json
# ...but result artefacts are committed; only transient run output is ignored.
!reports/phase_a_statistics.json
!reports/phase_a_tuning.json
!reports/phase_a_full_rf.json
!reports/phase_a2_tuning.json
!reports/phase_a2_hyperparameters.json
# Per-epoch validation curves. These are the evidence base for every claim
# about training budget - "the last 20 epochs gained +0.0007", "the best epoch
# was 529 of 800" - and none of it is checkable without them.
!reports/phase_a2_curves.json
!reports/steps_ladder_curves.json
# Archived artefacts of the invalidated 150-step run. Kept deliberately: the
# numbers must stay visible rather than disappear when they were withdrawn.
!reports/*_BROKEN_*.json
# Superseded tuning records, kept for the same reason. The cap-400 search is
# what showed the chosen hyperparameters depend on the cap - dual prefers
# dropout 0.3 at cap 400 and 0.1 at cap 800 - which is why tuning was repeated
# rather than carried over. Without these the decision is unauditable.
!reports/*_cap400.json
# The probe that settled whether cap 600 was adequate for both architectures.
!reports/cap600_adequacy_curves.json
!reports/.gitkeep

# Console logs of long runs. The substantive record is the JSON/CSV the run
# writes, which is committed; the log is the same information with timestamps
# and progress bars around it, and it grows every time a run is resumed.
reports/*.log
# Exception: the diagnostic probes print their results to stdout and write no
# CSV, so for them the log IS the substantive record rather than progress noise
# around it. The rule above assumes a run also writes structured output; these
# do not.
!reports/pooling_variants_probe.log
!reports/overfit_capacity_probe.log
!reports/factor_isolation_probe.log
!reports/pooling_fullscale_probe.log
!reports/steps_ladder_probe.log

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Transient run logs (regenerated by every run)
reports/*_log.txt

# External baseline implementations: cloned manually, not vendored.
external/*/
!external/README.mdvenv/
.env

# Transient run logs (regenerated by every run)
reports/*_log.txt

# External baseline implementations: cloned manually, not vendored.
external/*/
!external/README.md
